CAT = "sgm5Business"; SEG = "BUS"
Q = [
('Under section 36 of the FAA, a recommendation on an investment product must have:',
 'A reasonable basis', ['A guaranteed return', "The issuer's written approval", "A second adviser's sign-off"],
 "Section 36 of the FAA requires a reasonable basis for any recommendation to a person who may reasonably be expected to rely on it, having regard to the client's objectives, financial situation and needs."),
('A client who relied on a recommendation with no reasonable basis and lost money may:',
 'Bring a civil claim for the loss', ['Ask SGX to reverse the trade', 'Recover it from MAS', 'Claim only if the adviser is jailed'],
 'Section 36 can found a civil claim by a client who suffered loss. That is why FAA-N16 makes a financial adviser warn a client who chooses not to receive advice that he will not be able to rely on section 36 to file a civil claim.'),
('A representative tells a client that a fund "cannot lose money" when it can. This is:',
 'A false or misleading statement', ['Acceptable sales puffery', 'Fine if the fund did well last year', 'A matter only for the issuer'],
 'Section 35 of the FAA makes it an offence for a financial adviser to make false or misleading statements, or material omissions, with intent to deceive, about a contract for an investment product. Saying an investment cannot lose money when its value can fall misleads the client.'),
('An adviser that receives commission from product providers wants to call itself independent. Under the FAA it:',
 'May not use the word "independent"', ['May, if it discloses the commission', 'May, after MAS approval', 'May, if it sells two brands'],
 'Regulation 21 of the Financial Advisers Regulations bars the word "independent" unless the adviser receives no commission or other benefit from product providers that may create product bias, operates free of product restrictions and has no conflicting connection to a product provider.'),
('When recommending an investment product, a representative must disclose to the client:',
 'Its material information', ['Only the expected return', 'Only what the client asks', 'Only the brand of the issuer'],
 'Section 34 of the FAA requires a financial adviser to disclose to its clients information relating to an investment product it recommends, such as its terms, benefits, risks, fees and charges, and the product provider.'),
('An introducer who refers clients to a financial adviser must disclose to the client:',
 'Whether the adviser pays him', ['His own investment holdings', "The adviser's yearly profit", 'His home address'],
 'Under regulation 31 of the Financial Advisers Regulations, an introducer must tell clients that he may not give advice or arrange life policies, and whether he is paid by the financial adviser for the introduction, with the amount if the client asks.'),
("Who is liable for a representative's breach of the conduct rules while acting for his principal?",
 'Both the principal and him', ['Only the client who complained', 'Only the product issuer', 'No one, if it was honest'],
 "MAS's FAQs say financial advisers are responsible for the conduct of their representatives: they must report misconduct to MAS under FAA-N14 and take disciplinary action. The conduct sections also apply to the representative himself under section 46 of the FAA."),
('MAS believes a representative is no longer fit and proper. It can issue a:',
 'Prohibition order', ['Stop-trading notice to SGX', 'Writ of summons', 'Garnishee order'],
 'Under section 7(1) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022, MAS may issue a prohibition order if it is satisfied a person is not fit and proper, assessed against its Guidelines on Fit and Proper Criteria.'),
("A licensed financial adviser stops carrying on one of its regulated activities. It must notify MAS:",
 'Within 14 days', ['Within 6 months', 'Within 1 year', 'Only if MAS asks'],
 "Under section 14 of the FAA and regulation 12 of the Financial Advisers Regulations, a licensee notifies MAS on Form 5 within 14 days after ceasing any or all regulated activities."),
("The chief executive of a licensed financial adviser resigns. Under its licence conditions, the adviser must notify MAS:",
 'Immediately', ['Within 30 days', 'At its next annual return', 'Only if a client complains'],
 "MAS's Compliance Toolkit for Financial Advisers lists the resignation of the CEO or any director as a matter to notify MAS of immediately, under the licence conditions."),
("Section 38 of the FAA requires a financial adviser to:",
 'Give MAS information it asks for', ["Freeze a client's CPF account", 'Set fees that MAS approves', 'Get MAS approval for each sale'],
 'Section 38 requires a financial adviser to provide MAS with information about any matter related to its business, in Singapore or elsewhere, when MAS asks. MAS also inspects financial advisers.'),
('A licensed financial adviser must keep proper records of its business so that:',
 'Its dealings can be traced', ['Clients can browse other files', 'It can delete them after a year', 'Only its auditor sees them'],
 'Records let the adviser, its auditors and MAS trace and verify what was advised and transacted, which supports both supervision and complaint handling.'),
('A representative pressures a client to sign forms in blank so he can fill them later. This is:',
 'A serious breach of conduct', ['A normal time saver', 'Allowed if the client agrees', 'Allowed for repeat clients'],
 "Blank forms invite misrepresentation and remove the client's chance to check what is recorded, which goes against honest and fair dealing with the client."),
('Under the Financial Advisers (Complaints Handling and Resolution) Regulations 2021, a financial adviser reports on its complaints to MAS:',
 'Twice a year', ['Every month', 'Only when MAS asks', 'Once every three years'],
 'Regulation 9 requires the biannual complaints report (Form CHR) within 3 months after each half year ending 30 June or 31 December.'),
('A client cannot settle a dispute with his financial adviser. Which body offers independent mediation and adjudication?',
 'FIDReC', ['The Small Claims Tribunal only', 'The Singapore Exchange', 'The CPF Board'],
 'The Financial Industry Disputes Resolution Centre (FIDReC) is an independent body that helps resolve disputes between consumers and financial institutions, first by mediation and then, if no settlement is reached, by adjudication.'),
('Contravening a written direction from MAS, such as a notice issued under the FAA, is:',
 'An offence', ['Only a breach of contract', 'Only an internal matter', 'Allowed if no client lost money'],
 'Under section 67(5) of the FAA, contravening a requirement in a written direction from MAS, which includes its notices, is an offence punishable by a fine of up to S$25,000.'),
("A representative signs a client's name on a form to save time. This is:",
 'Forgery and misconduct', ['Acceptable with verbal consent', 'A minor admin lapse', 'Allowed for renewal forms'],
 'Signing for a client is dishonest and goes to honesty and integrity under the fit and proper criteria. The client must sign his own documents.'),
('A representative lends money to a client so the client can buy a policy. This is generally:',
 'A conflict of interest', ['Encouraged good service', 'Required for low-income clients', 'Allowed if repaid quickly'],
 "Financial dealings with clients, such as lending or borrowing money, create conflicts and pressure, which is why principals' codes of conduct generally forbid them."),
("A financial adviser's brochure recommends a unit trust in which the adviser has an interest. Under section 45 of the FAA, it must:",
 'Disclose its interest in that fund', ['Disclose all of its holdings', 'Say nothing about it', 'Have MAS approve the brochure'],
 "Section 45 requires a financial adviser to disclose its interests in a specified product in circulars or similar written communications, such as brochures, that recommend that product. It need not list its holdings in other products."),
('Before appointing a new chief executive officer, a licensed financial adviser must:',
 "Obtain MAS's approval", ['Inform its clients by letter', 'Register him with SGX', 'Wait for his first audit'],
 "Section 63(1) of the FAA, with regulation 13 of the Financial Advisers Regulations, requires MAS's approval (Form 11) before a CEO or director is appointed."),
]
